 "about": "COMPAT-CAH-DATA. Cases of the .ham/records locator and of the choice of the records folder, read by crates/agentd/tests/direct_records.rs, crates/ham-e2e/tests/lifecycle_layout.rs and scripts/tests/test_lifecycle_check.py and the tests of the scanner kit so the Rust reader, the scorer, the self-check script and the scanner kit give the same answer. `cases`: kind is default (the records sit in defaultBase/lifecycle, defaultBase/research and defaultBase/context), off, moved (dir is the folder that takes the place of defaultBase) or invalid; the value docs is a moved folder: it is the earlier layout of the default. `baseCases`: which folder is the base of the run, chosen once per run. A folder holds state when it is a real directory (no link) and holds a regular file named by stateFiles directly in it, or a regular file at any depth under a folder named by stateDirs (a link is nothing, an empty directory is nothing). Exactly one of the two folders holds state: that one is the base. Neither: the current folder. Both: refuse, and the message names both folders. expect is current, legacy or refuse. Each case builds its tree in an empty directory: files (a path, or a path with its text), emptyDirs and links (a path and the relative target it points to, which the case's files may fill).",
